{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144154-questions-about-garou-for-a-story","id":1144154,"title":"Questions about Garou for a story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-26T11:56:09-07:00","id":1144154,"title":"Questions about Garou for a story","content":"I have a crossover fanfiction that uses Garou. Though it doesn't use all aspects of Werewolf: the Apocalypse because it is a crossover with Buffy: tVS and has Xander go through a first change and become a Garou. The world is more like it is in Buffy, then the pre-apocalyptic world of Werewolf: tA. Though Buffy has it fair share of small to world ending apocalypses.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you want to check it out, it's on AO3, under the username TwistedImage and it is ch. 4 of a one-shot collection named Throw a Penny in the Wishing Well. I only have the beginning up and it was the very first draft of the story, so a good bit has been changed and re-worked since then. Mostly to do with the Umbra and interaction with Elder Garou, as I've done more research into Werewolf: The Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> \u200bI actually have some questions that maybe someone more familiar with the game could answer. I've tried to read as much as I can online but I didn't buy the books, since I was only doing research for the crossover. Which has spiraled out of control.<br /> <br /> \u200b1-Do Garou look different in the Penumbra/Umbra? I read somewhere that older souls (ones that have been reborn many times) that have done great or terrible deeds can have a reflection of that in the Umbra. Though I can't find where I read that and it may have been a person's own design, instead of canon to the games.<br /> <br /> \u200b2-What would the Sunnydale Hellmouth be? So far, I've just kept it as a portal into a hell dimension but the hell mouth monsters that come out of it will be 'wyrm' creatures, especially that multi-headed one that happens during mid-season 3 of Buffy. I'm trying to mix the lore a little from each.<br /> <br /> \u200b3-Some ideas on how to work banes, formori, and even BSDs into the story, along with the demons and Sunnydale vampires would be great. I've read somewhere that a certain type of bane was attracted to particularly vicious vampires and would increase such behavior.<br /> <br /> \u200b4-How long can a Homid Garou stay in Crinos form. In the storytelling form of the game, they stay in that form for a scene or so, to go along with the story. But I would imagine a newly turned Garou could only manage it for an hour or so? And as they get older and more experienced, be able to hold the change longer?<br /> <br /> \u200bI might have a few more but those are the top ones. I also posted something similar in the off-topic thread but it doesn't get near as much traffic, so decided to post something here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17550-twistedimage","name":"TwistedImage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:37:19-07:00","id":1144170,"title":"","content":"1 - Slightly, depending on their tribe and auspice. They will still be immediately recognizable.<br /> <br /> 2 - Well, Werewolf has things called Hellholes, and it has anchorheads to Malfeas that pop up. Those are rather serious business, and require some dedicated work to undo. Ultimately, it's your decision as to what you want it to be, but if you are doing a Werewolf crossover, it's that, or a Pit.<br /> <br /> 3 - Modern life leaves everyone with a bitter taste in their mouth about something. Banes sneak into these cracks and make their homes in them.<br /> <br /> 4 - As long as they want to. This isn't Werewolf: the Forsaken, there's no time limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T17:32:41-07:00","id":1144568,"title":"","content":"Thank you for answering.<br /> <br /> 1- In what ways? I had originally decided that Silver Fangs with many great deeds done by their soul would have wings in the Umbra and the same would be for Black Furies because of their tribal totem but have since removed that.<br /> <br /> \u200b2- I've looked into both but haven't really decided yet, though Pit matches better I believe. Hellhole doesn't exactly match since Sunnydale doesn't have a huge dump/nuclear waste site. Not all pits would have a pack of BSDs correct?<br /> <br /> \u200b3- Once a bane sneaks in, how long does it take for total possession to occur? And once that does occur, then the persons lifespan is limited, correct? I read that even a basic/delta class/common bane could shorten a life span to 5 years with a single point in the doomed category.<br /> <br /> \u200b4- Huh. I may still stick with the way I had originally planned to play it since it is a fanfiction. I had planned to make it harder for newly changed Garou to hold onto the Crinos form for extended time periods because of the rage and concentration it would take; though it would be easier the more rage they had (i.e: ahroun).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17550-twistedimage","user":"TwistedImage","date":". 09-27-2017, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17550-twistedimage","name":"TwistedImage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T20:20:00-07:00","id":1144615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwistedImage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144154-questions-about-garou-for-a-story?p=1144568#post1144568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for answering.<br /> <br /> 1- In what ways? I had originally decided that Silver Fangs with many great deeds done by their soul would have wings in the Umbra and the same would be for Black Furies because of their tribal totem but have since removed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>By canon, Umbra Revised detailed a kind of aura or what you could think of as a visual stylization. Moods are expressed more deeply and noticeably in appearance; I'd hate to relate it to slightly off-model reaction faces, but that might be slightly in the ballpark.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b2- I've looked into both but haven't really decided yet, though Pit matches better I believe. Hellhole doesn't exactly match since Sunnydale doesn't have a huge dump/nuclear waste site. Not all pits would have a pack of BSDs correct? </div> </div> </div>Hellholes can also result from atrocities and abuse, but in this case, if you want it to be very important to the plot, go with a Pit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b3- Once a bane sneaks in, how long does it take for total possession to occur? And once that does occur, then the persons lifespan is limited, correct? I read that even a basic/delta class/common bane could shorten a life span to 5 years with a single point in the doomed category. </div> </div> </div>It depends on how many successes on the Gnosis roll the bane got. This can range from six hours to the blink of an eye, and can be stopped through various means if not instantaneous. After that, a host can either accept taints in exchange for powers (which are not completely under the control of the bane; its nature dictates a lot of the character of a fomor), or else give up Autonomy (it's like Banality in reverse in terms of mechanics). Bottoming out on Autonomy means that the host gets absorbed and the being turns entirely into a bane. By the strict rules, Autonomy caps Willpower, but that should probably be a cap on effective Willpower to use against the bane's whims, as otherwise, the host can't really do much of anything against a character with mind control powers, which seems off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b4- Huh. I may still stick with the way I had originally planned to play it since it is a fanfiction. I had planned to make it harder for newly changed Garou to hold onto the Crinos form for extended time periods because of the rage and concentration it would take; though it would be easier the more rage they had (i.e: ahroun). </div> </div> </div>That's going to vastly change how any W:tA material shapes up. Crinos is easy to &quot;fall into&quot; by becoming enraged and flying utterly off the handle. It takes no focus to maintain it; maintaining it without going berserk, though, that's a bit of a tall order, as Crinos mechanically makes it easier to frenzy (-1 difficult to Rage rolls while in it). And given the way Rage works, you'll eventually fail, unless you're a Rank 6 Bringer of Light who has managed to gain extreme control after an important infiltration mission as a result of the Rite of Conquest (Shadow Lord version), at which point it will take 10 successes to frenzy on a Rage roll and more or less eliminates the dangers of Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies.<br /> <br /> Which are unfortunately named. Cuts out too much ambiguity where it needs to be, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}